    "md5": "89d8a8d3b59c18eef01d8387ced34973",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1895,
    "chunk_text": "Twelve standalone battery energy storage system projects for WindForce\n\nA top energy firm, WindForce, announced it has been awarded 12 standalone battery energy storage system (BESS) projects.\n\nThe total investment value for these 12 projects amounts to Rs 20.79\u202fbillion and project financing is expected to follow an 80:20 Debt-to-Equity structure.\n\n\u201cThe 12 projects collectively amount to a total installed capacity of 120\u202fMW/480MWh and will be developed as standalone BESS facilities under the Build, Own and Operate (BOO) model, operating over a 15\u2011year contract period, the company informed the CSE.\n\nOf the 12 projects, 11 will be fully owned and developed by WindForce, while the Vavunathivu project will be developed through a consortium between WindForce and Vidullanka.\n\nMeanwhile, CSE activities were extremely bullish and positive due to favourable earnings in quarterly results and also some media reports have revealed that SriLankan\u2019s economy is slowly but steadily stabilising.\n\nAmid those developments both indices moved upwards. The All Share Price Index went up by 199.71 points while the S and P SL20 rose by 97.18 points. Turnover stood at Rs 5.6 billion with eight crossings.\n\nTop seven crossings were reported in Seylan Bank (Non Voting) where 2.8 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 214 million; its shares traded at Rs 76, Dialog Axiata 5.4 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 177 million; its shares sold at Rs 33, JKH 3.5 million shares crossed for Rs 78 million; its shares traded at Rs 22.30, Sampath Bank 450,000 shares crossed for Rs 70.32 million; its shares sold at Rs 156, Cargills Bank three million shares crossed for Rs 27.9 million; its shares traded at Rs 9.30, ACL Cables 248,000 shares crossed for Rs 24.8 million; its shares sold at Rs 100 and Commercial Bank 100,000 shares crossed for Rs 23.2 million; its shares sold at Rs 232.50."
