    "chunk_size_bytes": 1121,
    "chunk_text": "Unavoidable circumstances \u2026\n\nThe \u2018ROCK meets REGGAE\u2019 concert, scheduled for 28th February, has been rescheduled, due to unavoidable circumstances, as mentioned by Rohitha Jayalath, of JAYASRI fame, on social media: \u201cWe\u2019ve rescheduled the event! New date coming soon. Refunds available \u2026.\u201d\n\nRock and reggae music fans were looking forward to this event as the lineup included Sri Lanka\u2019s rock star Chitral Somapala, together with Black Majesty (from Australia) and the band JAYASRI.\n\nThe last ROCK meets REGGAE event was held in Colombo in 2019; in general, rock and reggae music fans have very little to look forward to in the scene here.\n\nAccording to reports, Austria\u2019s biggest Reggae Festival is coming up in August, this year \u2013 7th and 8th August \u2013 with a very strong lineup, and JAYASRI is in the scene, as well.\n\nAlpha Blondy, who did his thing in Colombo, last year, is also a part of the programme.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
