    "md5": "f976c49ff0d0c9753ccb08225c81e6bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1949,
    "chunk_text": "Official Olympic flooring provider, Gerflor partners with WIDAC Commercial Interiors to introduce world-class solutions to Sri Lanka\n\nFrom left: Gerflor Asia Specification Consultant Sathya Kumar; Gerflor Asia Regional Sales Head Benjamin Le Toux; Director Tarusha Weerasooria; and Business Head \u2013 Interior Solutions Division Kumudu Vithanaarachchi.\n\nWIDAC Commercial Interiors has announced its official partnership with Gerflor, a global leader in specialised flooring solutions, marking a significant step forward for the Sri Lankan commercial interiors market.\n\nThrough this collaboration, WIDAC Commercial Interiors will introduce Gerflor\u2019s internationally recognised flooring systems to Sri Lanka, with a strong focus on sports flooring and hospital flooring, two segments where performance, safety, and durability are critical. The partnership brings proven global solutions to local institutions, enabling projects to meet international standards while responding to the practical demands of high-traffic environments.\n\nWith more than 37 years of experience, over 2,000 completed projects, 3,000 clients, and more than 5 million square feet of interiors delivered, WIDAC Commercial Interiors has established itself as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most trusted commercial interior solution providers. Known for its integrated approach spanning design, supply, and execution, WIDAC continues to expand its portfolio with partners that share its commitment to quality and long-term performance.\n\nGerflor, headquartered in France and present in more than 100 countries, is globally respected for its innovation in resilient flooring systems designed for professional environments. Its solutions are widely used in sports facilities, hospitals, educational institutions, and public buildings, spaces where safety, hygiene, and durability cannot be compromised. Notably, Gerflor has been the official flooring supplier to the Olympic Games since 1976."
  },
