    "md5": "7e1fd4fcfacc23a0bd4eabee1f438ed7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka Hospitals secures third consecutive Gold award at 60th anniversary TAGS\n\nLanka Hospitals finance and management team at the event. From left: Lanka Hospitals Senior Executive \u2013 Finance Madushan Kavishka, Lanka Hospitals Senior Manager \u2013 Legal and Compliance Ama Wimalasena, Finance Manager Kasun Gimhan Perera; Lanka Hospitals Group Group Chief Financial Officer M.B.G. Wickramasiri, Group Managing Director Chaaminda Kumarasiri; Lanka Hospitals Senior Manager \u2013 Finance Harsha Deeptha, Assistant Accountant Dilanka Jayathunga, Diagnostics Senior Manager \u2013 Finance Chalitha Abeydeera, Executive \u2013 Finance Kanishka Sampath; and Senior Executive \u2013 Finance Lakshika Samarasinghe\n\nLanka Hospitals PLC has secured the Gold Award in the Health Sector at the prestigious TAGS Awards 2025. This historic achievement marks the third consecutive year the institution has been recognised for its world-class reporting standards, a feat that coincides with the 60th \u201cDiamond Chapter\u201d anniversary of the awards organised by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka).\n\nUnder the theme \u201cDiamond Chapter: The Grand Honour of Excellence,\u201d the 2025 TAGS Awards represent a sixty-year legacy of benchmarking Transparency, Accountability, Governance, and Sustainability. In an era of heightened stakeholder expectations, Lanka Hospitals\u2019 sustained dominance in this category validates a reporting culture that is not just compliant, but transformative.\n\nThe recognition serves as an independent validation of Lanka Hospitals\u2019 commitment to building trust through absolute clarity. By presenting a fair, balanced, and forward-looking account of its performance, the hospital ensures that stakeholders\u2014from investors to the patients who rely on its care\u2014can engage with the institution with unwavering confidence."
  },
