    "chunk_text": "The recognition serves as an independent validation of Lanka Hospitals\u2019 commitment to building trust through absolute clarity. By presenting a fair, balanced, and forward-looking account of its performance, the hospital ensures that stakeholders\u2014from investors to the patients who rely on its care\u2014can engage with the institution with unwavering confidence.\n\nThe 2025 awards, which for the first time integrated advanced AI-driven evaluation criteria, assessed organisations on the quality, clarity, and credibility of their annual reports. For Lanka Hospitals, this win highlights the robustness of its governance disclosures and the integrity of its financial information.\n\nGroup Chief Financial Officer M.B.G. Wickramasiri said: \u201cWinning the Gold award for the third consecutive year is an affirmation of the rigour we apply to our financial stewardship. In a complex economic environment, we have remained steadfast in our dedication to best-in-class corporate governance. Transparency is more than a duty; it is a core value that ensures our accountability to our shareholders, our investors, and the Sri Lankan public.\u201d\n\nLanka Hospitals continues to set new standards in the healthcare sector, underpinned by its prestigious Joint Commission International (JCI) accreditation \u2014 the globally recognised gold standard in healthcare quality and patient safety \u2014 and the distinction of being the first medical institution in Sri Lanka to be reaccredited by JCI. From earning the prestigious College of American Pathologists (CAP) accreditation for its laboratory network to pioneering \u201cNext Gen Healing\u201d through cutting-edge medical technology, the hospital\u2019s operational success is mirrored in its reporting excellence.\n\nThe award was received on behalf of the Lanka Hospitals team by Group Managing Director Chaaminda Kumarasiri and Group Chief Financial Officer M.B.G. Wickramasiri at a grand finale held at the Shangri-La, Colombo."
