    "language": "en",
    "md5": "209b75501c131c5b9374f09edecf6f3e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1639,
    "chunk_text": "BIOFACH 2026: A gateway for Sri Lanka\u2019s organic export expansion\n\nBIOFACH, being the world\u2019s largest and most influential international trade fair dedicated to the organic sector, provides a vital global platform for countries to promote their certified organic products and strengthen their presence in international markets.\n\nRecognising this importance, Sri Lanka will participate in BIOFACH 2026, to be held in Nuremberg, Germany, from 10-13 February 2026, with a strong national presence organised by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) in collaboration with the National Organic Control Unit (NOCU).\n\nThe EDB will organise a Sri Lanka Country Pavilion, featuring a large and prominently located stall, with the participation of eight leading Sri Lankan organic exporters: Mico Ceylon Organics Ltd., WICHY Plantation Ltd., Elhena Agro Ltd., Peoples Organisation for Development Import & Export (PODIE), Ceylon Eco Spices Ltd., Ceylon Exports & Trading Ltd., Bespice Ltd., and Peal Isle Foods Exports Ltd. These companies will be provided with a valuable opportunity to display their products and engage directly with international buyers at this prestigious global trade event.\n\nBIOFACH brings together exhibitors and trade visitors from all parts of the world to explore the latest developments, innovations, and emerging trends in organic food and related sectors. In addition to being a marketplace, the exhibition offers extensive opportunities for networking, business matchmaking, and knowledge exchange through its supporting programs, including the BIOFACH congress, forums, trend sessions, and innovation stages."
  },
