    "md5": "72944673424ee10c68471254f998dbb4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1772,
    "chunk_text": "BIOFACH brings together exhibitors and trade visitors from all parts of the world to explore the latest developments, innovations, and emerging trends in organic food and related sectors. In addition to being a marketplace, the exhibition offers extensive opportunities for networking, business matchmaking, and knowledge exchange through its supporting programs, including the BIOFACH congress, forums, trend sessions, and innovation stages.\n\nA dedicated promotional corner will highlight organic products from small and medium-scale enterprises (SMEs). And this Virtual SME Corner will feature 10 SME companies, enabling wider representation of Sri Lanka\u2019s organic sector and providing them with international visibility.\n\nIn parallel, an awareness campaign on Sri Lanka Organic will be conducted to promote the Sri Lanka Organic Standard (SLS 1324) and the National Regulatory Framework governing organic production and certification.\n\nAdding further value to the Sri Lanka Pavilion, live food demonstrations will be conducted for three consecutive days commencing from 10 February, showcasing the versatility and quality of Sri Lankan organic ingredients. In addition, Pure Ceylon Tea tasting sessions will be offered throughout the exhibition, allowing visitors to experience the distinctive flavour and premium quality of Sri Lanka\u2019s world-renowned tea.\n\nDuring the event, the EDB and NOCU will also engage in discussions with international bodies such as the UK Department for Environment, Food & Rural Affairs (DEFRA) and the United Kingdom Trade Partnership (UKTP) with a view to strengthening cooperation, uplifting Sri Lanka\u2019s organic standards, and further improving the country\u2019s organic regulatory framework in line with international best practices."
