    "md5": "992e896d9c28061c9c0cb2e1bb22ad0e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "Seylan Bank appoints two new directors\n\nSeylan Bank PLC has further strengthened its Board of Directors with the appointment of two veteran professionals, W.D. Batagoda as a Non-Executive Director with effect from 26 December 2025, and Ramani Samarasundera as an Independent Non-Executive Director with effect from 26 January 2026.\n\nW.D. Batagoda is an Attorney-at-Law with nearly two decades of experience in criminal law, public law, and fundamental rights, having practiced in both appellate and original courts. He holds an LL.B. and LLM from the University of Colombo and is currently reading for his Ph.D. in Law at the same university.\n\nBatagoda, since joining the LOLC Group in 2014, has held senior leadership positions at LOLC Holdings PLC. He is Chief Legal Officer of LOLC Holdings PLC and holds directorships in several LOLC Group companies including Non-Executive Chairman of Browns Development Limited, and Non-Executive Director of Gal Oya Plantation Limited, Fortigrains Private Limited (Singapore), Fortigrains Lanka Private Limited, Ceylon Nano \u2013 Diagnostic (Pvt) Ltd., LOLC Asset Holdings Limited, Leapstitch Apparel (Pvt) Ltd., LOLC Geo Technologies (Pvt) Ltd., Browns Agri Solutions (Private) Limited, Browns Properties (Private) Limited, and LOLC (Philippines) Corporation.\n\nHe functioned as Chairperson of the Corporate Lawyers\u2019 Committee of the Bar Association of Sri Lanka from 2021 to 2022 and as Non-Executive, Non-Independent Director of DFCC Bank from September 2022 to December 2024.\n\nRamani Samarasundera possesses over 30 years of experience in marketing, brand building, and consumer insight-driven growth across leading FMCG organizations. She holds a Bachelor of Science degree with First Class Honours from the University of Colombo, where she topped her batch."
