    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "Celebrating Sri Lanka \u2018Jayaflava\u2019 way\n\nFirst ever Sri Lankan six-part food and travel series premiers on National Geographic South Asia tomorrow\n\nA HarperCollins-Published Author and Sri Lankan Food Storyteller Tasha Marikkar\n\nCinnamon Hotels and Resorts Colombo City Hotels Vice President and Cinnamon Life General Manager Kamal Munasinghe\n\nCinnamon Hotels and Resorts Vice President and Brand Excellence Brandon Ingram\n\nDentsu Grant Communications Planning and Media Strategy Vice President Bakmee Perera\n\nA Sri Lankan\u2019s love letter to her resplendent isle, \u201cJayaflava: celebrating Sri Lanka\u201d, will explode onto South Asian televisions spotlight, as a six-part food and travel series, told through a lense of authentic Sri Lankan food, venturing to touch the core of the country while embodying her flavours, culture, people and generosity of spirit.\n\nInspired by Sri Lankan food storyteller Tasha Marikkar\u2019s Harper Collins published cookbook, Jayaflava, the series will be hosted by Marikkar herself and directed by Afdhel Aziz, who will continue his stories of all things proudly local, following the cinematic triumph of \u201cThe Genius of the Place\u201d his documentary on Geoffrey Bawa.\n\n\u201cJayaflava has been a mad, chaotic, fun and slightly unhinged journey but also a real eye opener and I envisioned my Sri Lankan cookbook to be real and not diluted nor apologetic and represent my home as I knew it- multi-ethnic, modern, generous, opinionated and completely obsessed with flavour. The birth of the TV series stemmed from my realisation that I should focus beyond the recipes, to the streets where koththu was chopped at midnight, the village kitchens, bars and beaches that breathe the soul of Sri Lanka,\u201d Marikkar explained at the media conference held at Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams on Tuesday."
  },
