    "chunk_index": 4,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9b7d693d7f6f97406b8d4f27a535389d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1028,
    "chunk_text": "Families live in prolonged fear, children\u2019s schooling and mental health have unravelled, and rituals tied to land and the dead remain incomplete, yet these harms are absent from official assessments and narratives. National and international frameworks, including UNDP and World Bank assessments, focus on what can be measured and monetised, while ignoring grief, trauma, cultural erosion, and the breakdown of social cohesion.\n\nThe government should stop fooling itself and the people of Sri Lanka by facing reality and demanding greater debt relief. Auditing for illegitimate debt, curbing illicit financial flows, and closing tax loopholes for the corporate sector, will strengthen the fiscal capabilities of the government in the short and medium term.\n\nSri Lanka is locked on an IMF-dependent path. This leads in only one direction: a new IMF program with added austerities after 2027. The best sympathy and solidarity Kristalina Georgieva can give the people of Sri Lanka is for the IMF to take its hands off our future."
  },
