    "md5": "cd3b1b86a30d8ae146b197bfb809ec85",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1173,
    "chunk_text": "EDB opens doors for Southern Province exporters at Matara Networking Forum next week\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) is set to host the Southern Province Regional Exporters\u2019 Networking Forum on 24 February in Matara.\n\nThe primary objective of the forum is to identify the challenges faced by regional exporters, empower them, and explore new opportunities for growth.\n\nExporters and Government officials representing the districts of Galle, Matara, Hambantota, and Monaragala are expected to participate in the event.\n\nThe Forum will be presided over by Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunneththi, and will provide a unique platform for exporters to directly present their concerns to the Minister and engage in open dialogue.\n\nHeads of relevant Government institutions as well as Export Development Officers attached to district and Divisional Secretariat offices will also be in attendance, with the aim of providing swift solutions to exporters\u2019 issues.\n\nTo ensure more productive discussions, the Southern Province Office of the EDB has already begun collecting specific concerns and proposals from exporters in the region."
