    "md5": "2587553925d30246b9de699287a75b27",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1337,
    "chunk_text": "Lankan envoy in Pakistan meets Habib Bank Chairman\n\nThe High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to Pakistan Fred Senevirathne, met with the Habib Bank Ltd., (HBL) Chairman Sultan Ali Allana, at the Chairman\u2019s office on 7 February. The High Commissioner was accompanied by Head of Chancery Christy Ruban, Honorary Consul of Sri Lanka in Hyderabad Mehmood Mandviwalla, and Consul General of Sri Lanka in Karachi.\n\nDuring the meeting, the High Commissioner conveyed his sincere appreciation to the Chairman and Habib Bank Ltd., for their generous contribution towards relief efforts following the recent devastating floods in Sri Lanka. He expressed the gratitude of the Government and the people of Sri Lanka for this timely and meaningful humanitarian assistance.\n\nThe Chairman Allana recalled HBL\u2019s long-standing presence in Colombo, spanning several decades, and reaffirmed the bank\u2019s continued commitment to strengthening its engagement with Sri Lanka. He underscored the enduring friendship between Pakistan and Sri Lanka and expressed his intention to visit Sri Lanka in the near future.\n\nThe meeting was held in a warm and cordial atmosphere. Both sides reaffirmed the strong bilateral relations between Pakistan and Sri Lanka and expressed their shared commitment to further enhancing cooperation, goodwill, and people-to-people ties."
  },
