    "md5": "4af3e65591a74b7806b975daf291813f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1895,
    "chunk_text": "Abans Environmental Services sets new ethical benchmark as Sri Lanka\u2019s first facility services provider to achieve SEDEX/SMETA\n\nIn a significant milestone for Sri Lanka\u2019s facility services industry, Abans Environmental Services Ltd., has become the first company in the sector to achieve SEDEX membership and align with the globally recognised SMETA audit framework, setting a new benchmark for ethical, transparent, and sustainable business practices.\n\nThe SMETA verification was independently conducted by Control Union, a globally respected certification and verification body, providing strong third-party assurance of the company\u2019s compliance with international standards covering labour practices, health and safety, environmental responsibility, and business ethics.\n\nThis achievement places Abans Environmental Services at the forefront of responsible business conduct in Sri Lanka\u2019s facility services sector. By embracing SEDEX/SMETA, the company goes beyond compliance\u2014demonstrating leadership in uplifting industry standards and championing ethical practices across operations and supply chains.\n\nEstablished in 1985 and operating as part of the diversified Abans Group, Abans Environmental Services has built a reputation for reliability, professionalism, and operational excellence. For nearly four decades, the company has supported organisations across Sri Lanka by delivering integrated janitorial and facility management solutions that contribute to cleaner, healthier, and safer environments.\n\nIts comprehensive service portfolio includes professional janitorial and cleaning services, tea services, pest control, and specialised cleaning solutions to commercial, industrial, institutional, and public-sector clients. With a skilled workforce and strong operational systems, the company continues to set high benchmarks in service quality, safety, and sustainability."
  },
