    "chunk_size_bytes": 1765,
    "chunk_text": "Singer Sri Lanka honoured for ethical business practices\n\nSinger Sri Lanka PLC has been awarded the Gold Award in the Trading Companies category at an awards ceremony organized by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka, recognizing the pinnacle of corporate reporting achievement in the country.\n\nThe Gold Award is a powerful endorsement of Singer\u2019s robust corporate governance framework and its unwavering commitment to transparency, accountability, and ethical business practices. The accolade highlights the company\u2019s leadership in sustainability and responsible retailing, from strengthening community initiatives to embedding sustainable operations across its island-wide network.\n\nMahesh Wijewardene, Group Managing Director, stated: \u201cThis Gold Award is a reflection of the disciplined governance culture we have embedded across the Singer Group. Transparency and accountability are not compliance requirements for us\u2014they are core principles that guide every strategic decision we make.\u201d\n\nAs a market leader in Sri Lanka\u2019s retail and trading sector, the win reinforces Singer\u2019s ability to integrate sound financial management with innovative trading excellence. With this latest milestone, Singer continues to strengthen its position as one of the country\u2019s most respected organizations, setting new benchmarks in corporate accountability and sustainable growth.\n\nUniversity of Surrey launches Asia\u2019s first Master\u2019s in Digital Health at IIHS, Sri Lanka\n\nSeeing is believing \u2013 the silent scale behind SriLankan\u2019s ground operation\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
