    "chunk_size_bytes": 1734,
    "chunk_text": "Casons Rent A Car unveils new luxury fleet for premium travel\n\nCasons Rent A Car has announced a major investment in a fully owned fleet of brand-new luxury vehicles, marking a first for Sri Lanka\u2019s premium mobility sector. The enhanced offering features carefully handpicked models, including the Toyota Land Cruiser LC 300, Range Rover Sport, Toyota Alphard Executive Lounge, Mercedes-Benz Sprinter, and a luxury Higer 50-seater.\n\n\u201cThese vehicles were purchased recently, are unmarked, and are fully owned by us,\u201d a company official confirmed. \u201cWe do not borrow fleets or depend on third-party vehicles. This ensures the highest standards of safety, reliability, and service consistency.\u201d\n\nBy retaining full ownership, Casons said it maintains strict operational control, professional maintenance, and guaranteed vehicle availability without last-minute substitutions. The fleet is available for short-term rentals, corporate assignments, and exclusive travel requirements.\n\n\u201cWith this addition, we are well-positioned to handle mega projects, official delegations, foreign missions, and upscale events,\u201d the official added. \u201cOur clients deserve more than transportation \u2013 they deserve confidence, comfort, and complete peace of mind.\u201d\n\nThe investment strengthens Casons\u2019 position as a leader in Sri Lanka\u2019s high-end travel sector.\n\nComBank\u2019s \u2018Pita Rata Wasi\u2019 remittance promo back with Rs. 6 million in cash prizes\n\nUniversity of Surrey launches Asia\u2019s first Master\u2019s in Digital Health at IIHS, Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
