    "md5": "2b55c3868edc49547e2de995cab2dd4a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1491,
    "chunk_text": "University of Surrey launches Asia\u2019s first Master\u2019s in Digital Health at IIHS, Sri Lanka\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s International Institute of Health Sciences (IIHS) has launched Asia\u2019s first Master\u2019s in Digital Health awarded by the University of Surrey, UK. The programme addresses the growing global demand for professionals who can integrate technology and data into healthcare delivery.\n\nDelivered at IIHS in Colombo, the curriculum covers digital health systems, informatics, data analytics, and emerging technologies. It is designed for doctors, nurses, health administrators, IT graduates, and other professionals seeking leadership roles in digital health. No prior technical expertise is required.\n\nDr. Kithsiri Edirisinghe, CEO of IIHS, stated: \u201cDigital Health is essential to the future of healthcare. By delivering Asia\u2019s first University of Surrey Master\u2019s in Digital Health, we are creating opportunities for graduates and professionals to access global careers.\u201d\n\nGraduates can pursue roles including Digital Health Specialist, Health Informatics Manager, and Telemedicine Lead. The launch reinforces Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a hub for international healthcare education under the \u201cStudy Sri Lanka\u201d initiative.\n\nCasons Rent A Car unveils new luxury fleet for premium travel\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
