    "md5": "93db017678a283bbd77f137d942c9a99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1907,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWildlife is not separate from us. It is part of the same ecological system that sustains human life,\u201d she said. \u201cWorld Wildlife Day reminds us that every species plays a role in maintaining balance. When we lose wildlife, we lose part of the natural system that supports our own survival.\u201d\n\nHer words echo with quiet conviction, shaped by years of engagement with Sri Lanka\u2019s natural heritage and the mounting pressures it faces.\n\nSri Lanka became a signatory to the convention in 1978, affirming its commitment to conservation and international cooperation.\n\nSince then, the Department of Wildlife Conservation has served as the guardian of the island\u2019s wild spaces. Its officers patrol remote forests, monitor wildlife populations, combat illegal trade, and work tirelessly to protect fragile ecosystems.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s wildlife faces a complex web of threats\u2014habitat loss, climate change, illegal poaching, pollution, and human encroachment. Expanding settlements and infrastructure have fragmented habitats that animals have used for centuries. Climate shifts alter rainfall patterns, affecting food availability and breeding cycles. Illegal wildlife trade continues to target vulnerable species.\n\nYet despite these pressures, Sri Lanka remains one of the most biologically rich nations on Earth.\n\nThe island is home to iconic species, such as the Sri Lankan elephant, the Sri Lankan leopard, and countless endemic birds, reptiles, and amphibians. Many of these species exist nowhere else, making their survival a global responsibility.\n\nSarathchandra stressed the importance of public awareness and participation in conservation.\n\n\u201cConservation cannot be achieved by government institutions alone,\u201d she said. \u201cIt requires the support of communities, the involvement of young people, and a national commitment to protecting our natural heritage. Every citizen has a role to play.\u201d"
  },
