    "chunk_text": "ComBank wins 5 including double Gold at CA Sri Lanka TAGS Awards 2025\n\nReinforcing the Bank\u2019s commitment to upholding the highest standards of corporate reporting and best governance practices, the Commercial Bank of Ceylon has won five major awards including two Golds at the 2025 TAGS Awards of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka), demonstrating its strong focus on Transparency, Accountability, Governance, and Sustainability.\n\nPresented at a ceremony at the Shangri-La Hotel, Colombo, the awards recognise the Bank\u2019s 2024 Annual Report titled \u2018In Context \u2013 From turbulence towards tranquility\u2019 for excellence in disclosure across multiple dimensions of transparency and governance.\n\nCommercial Bank received the Overall Silver award for Excellence in Corporate Reporting, underscoring the strength and comprehensiveness of its financial reporting. The Bank also clinched the Gold award as the winner in the Banking Sector and a second Gold for Corporate Governance in the Financial Services Sector under the Special Awards Category.\n\nFurther affirming the robustness and clarity of its integrated disclosures, the Bank won the Silver award for Integrated Reporting in the Special Award Category, and a Bronze award for Digitally Transformative Reporting, another Special Award Category."
