    "chunk_text": "MGR enticed Jayalalithaa into his party in 1982 and launched her on a successful political career by making her Propaganda Secretary and Rajya Sabha (Upper House) MP. With MGR\u2019s blessings Jayalalithaa blossomed into a formidable politician. After MGR\u2019s death in 1987, she wrested full control of the party in 1989 and led the AIADMK to victory two years later.MGR had been called \u201cPuratchi Thalaiver\u201d or Revolutionary Leader. Jayalalithaa became known by the feminine equivalent of revolutionary leader \u2013 \u201cPuratchi Thalaivi\u201d.\n\nThis article  originally written for the \u201cSpotlight\u201d Column appears in the \u201cDaily FT\u201d of December 17, 2016. It can be accessed here: http://www.ft.lk/article/586033/When-actress-Jayalalithaa-reigned\u2013as-uncrowned-Queen-of-Tamil-cinema\n\nFebruary 2014: Tamil Nadu Chief Minister J Jayalalithaa serves food while inaugurating a new canteen set up by Chennai Corporation in which food will be provided at subsidised rates in Chennai \u2013 PTI\n\nA file picture of Tamil Nadu Chief Minister Jayalalithaa at a function in Chennai. Photo: M. Vedhan-courtesy: The Hindu"
