    "chunk_size_bytes": 1779,
    "chunk_text": "SLIIT team secures global title at International Business Plan Competition 2025 in South Korea\n\nThe Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology (SLIIT) has achieved a historic international milestone as a team of undergraduate students from the SLIIT Business School secured the World Championship at the International Business Plan Competition (IBPC) 2025, hosted by SolBridge International School of Business of Woosong University in Daejeon, South Korea. The achievement marks a defining moment for Sri Lankan business education on the global stage and positions SLIIT among the world\u2019s leading institutions in business innovation and strategy.\n\nEstablished in 2013, IBPC is a globally recognised annual competition that brings together leading universities from around the world to tackle real-world business challenges. The 2025 edition featured a rigorous multi-stage process, beginning with an international online qualifying round and culminating in the in-person global finals held from January 26 to 30, 2026, in South Korea. Universities from across Asia, Europe, and the Americas competed in what is widely regarded as one of the most demanding undergraduate business case competitions.\n\nThis year\u2019s challenge, developed in collaboration with Lake Materials Co., Ltd., a leading Korean chemical materials manufacturer, required teams to craft a comprehensive strategy for sustainable growth from an Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) perspective. Participants were tasked with analysing the company\u2019s strategic position and proposing innovative, financially viable, and sustainable solutions aligned with global ESG standards. The case demanded not only analytical excellence but also practical implementation planning and robust financial modelling."
