    "chunk_text": "In the retail market top seven companies that have mainly contributed to the turnover were ACL Cables Rs 268.7 million (2.6 million shares traded), Asia Siyaka Rs 246.9 million (14 million shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 158.3 million (two million shares traded), Acme Printers Rs 94.8 million (30.8 million shares traded), JKH Rs 92.9 million (4.2 million shares traded),Colombo Dockyards Rs 84.5 million (551,000 shares traded) and Sampath Bank Rs 84 million (518,000 shares traded). During the day 152.5 million shares volumes changed hands in 31244 transactions.\n\nYesterday the Central Bank announced the US Dollar rate as against rupee. The rupee was quoted at Rs 309.35/40 to the US dollar in the spot market, from Rs. 309.36/38 the previous day, dealers said, while bond yields edged up slightly.\n\nSteps leading to the achievement of SL\u2019s national interest in IOR\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
