    "chunk_text": "Aitken Spence Chairperson Stasshani Jayawardena to assume interim Managing Director role\n\nAitken Spence PLC has appointed its Executive Chairperson Stasshani Jayawardena as the interim Managing Director of the company with effect from 1 April 2026.\n\nJayawardena is graduate of St. James\u2019 and Lucie Clayton College and Keele University in the United Kingdom, Emeritus Institute of Management, Singapore \u2013 and an Associate Alumni of University of Cambridge (Judge Business School), United Kingdom.\n\nJayawardena marks several milestones as the first female Chairperson of Aitken Spence Hotel Holdings PLC and of Aitken Spence PLC in its 156-year history with her appointment as Executive Chairperson in February 2025. She was the youngest and first female Board member of Aitken Spence PLC, Aitken Spence Hotel Holdings PLC, and Browns Beach Hotels PLC in December 2013.\n\nWith a career spanning over 10 years at Aitken Spence, she wields a fresh perspective in management and leads strategic business units across the group. She leads several key strategic teams as the Chairperson of Aitken Spence Hotel Managements Ltd., Deputy Chairperson of Lanka Milk Foods (CWE) PLC, as a member on the Board of Directors of Stassen Group, Melstacorp PLC and Distilleries Company of Sri Lanka PLC.\n\nJayawardena was the youngest intern to work under US Senator Hilary Rodham Clinton and the Former US President Bill Clinton in 2003; and was appointed as the Sri Lankan Ambassador for EY NextGen Club from 2017 to 2019. She is also a member of the PwC NextGen Advisory Council since 2020."
  },
