    "chunk_text": "Capt. (Retd.) Jagmohan serves as Chairman and Managing Director of the Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders Ltd. (MDL). He is a Naval Architect from Cochin University of Science and Technology. He has also done post-graduation and M. Tech in Naval Construction and Ocean Engineering from IIT Delhi and IIT Kharagpur, respectively. He served for over 25 years in the Indian Navy during which he held several important assignments in the Directorate of Naval Design and at Naval Dockyard, Mumbai. Prior to joining MDL, he was Director (Corporate Planning, Project and Business Development) and Director (Operations) - Addl. Charge at Goa Shipyard Ltd. He also worked with Garden Reach Shipbuilders and\u00a0 Engineers Ltd. (GRSE), Kolkata as Chief General Manager (Design). As Head of Design at GRSE, he was responsible for the execution and management of design of various complex warship projects such as Advanced Stealth Frigate, P28 ASW Corvette, Survey Vessel, ASW Shallow Water Craft and Fast Patrol Vessels for the Indian Navy & Indian Coast Guard.\n\nRuchir Agrawal serves as the Director (Finance) of MDL, one of India\u2019s premier Defence Public Sector Undertakings. His appointment approved by the Appointments Committee of the Cabinet (ACC) stands as a testament to his exceptional professional credibility and the Government of India\u2019s confidence in his financial leadership. He also functions as the Chief Financial Officer (CFO) and Chief Information and Security Officer (CISO) of the company, shaping MDL\u2019s strategic direction through his active role in several Board-level committees, including the CSR, Stakeholder relationship and the Risk Management Committee.\n\nA Fellow Member of both the Institute of Cost and Works Accountants of India (ICWAI) and the Institute of Chartered Shipbrokers, London, Agrawal brings a rare blend of financial expertise, maritime knowledge, and strategic foresight."
