    "chunk_text": "All that the aircraft owners and operators are asking for is replacement of the concrete wall with a less hazardous frangible (breaking on impact), transparent fence. With proper signage and warnings for road users, an observant motor vehicle driver could brake and stop in time to prevent collision with an uncontrolled, over-running aircraft that can be seen from a distance, thus providing adequate warning of imminent danger.\n\nOver the past 20 years, the civil aviation authorities have done nothing to mitigate threats and hazards at Ratmalana Airport. Expert advice has fallen on deaf ears. Instead, administrators have created more problems for themselves. They have even demolished a part of the iconic terminal building built in the 1950s, in the name of progress. That is another story!\n\nRCyAF/SLAF, Air Ceylon, Air Lanka, Singapore Airlines & SriLankan Airlines.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
