    "chunk_size_bytes": 1995,
    "chunk_text": "Scale Up 2026 10th anniversary brings over 50 global partners to Colombo\n\nLeading European technology and finance organisations among those at launch of Gapstars Group\n\nScale Up 2026 recently marked 10 years of Gapstars building high-performance embedded teams from Sri Lanka and introduced a new chapter with the formal launch of Gapstars Group in a milestone event in global collaboration in Colombo.\n\nHeld from 2-6 February, the week brought together more than 50 international partners representing leading European technology and finance organisations. For many, it was not their first visit. Several have spent years building embedded Sri Lankan teams that now play a central role in product innovation, enterprise systems, and financial operations across Europe and beyond.\n\nScale Up was not designed as a traditional conference. Instead, it functioned as a working summit \u2013 combining Artificial Intelligence (AI) workshops, agile collaboration sessions, intercultural leadership modules, and teambuilding activities. Founders, CTOs, IT directors, and finance leaders worked side by side with their Sri Lankan counterparts to review roadmaps, refine financial structures, and accelerate delivery.\n\nThe defining announcement of the week was the launch of Gapstars Group, uniting its established technology vertical with its expanding finance capability under one integrated structure. After a decade focused on engineering and product teams, the organisation has formalised its finance vertical, embedding Sri Lankan professionals into European companies across reporting, compliance, controls, and forecasting functions.\n\nGapstars Co-Founder Hugo Hemmen said: \u201cOur first decade was about proving that distributed engineering teams from Sri Lanka could operate at global standards. The next decade is about scale, across technology and finance. We are not building support functions; we are building high-performance teams that operate at the heart of our partners\u2019 organisations.\u201d"
