    "chunk_text": "Gapstars Co-Founder Hugo Hemmen said: \u201cOur first decade was about proving that distributed engineering teams from Sri Lanka could operate at global standards. The next decade is about scale, across technology and finance. We are not building support functions; we are building high-performance teams that operate at the heart of our partners\u2019 organisations.\u201d\n\nBrompton, the UK-based certified B Corp and globally recognised brand, was recognised as Partner of the Year for its sustained collaboration and growth within its Sri Lankan engineering team.\n\nBrompton Team in Sri Lanka Head of Analytics Dilraj Sura said: \u201cWhat makes this partnership strong is ownership. Our team is not working on isolated tasks, we\u2019re contributing to decisions, architecture, and long-term product direction. Scale Up strengthens that alignment face-to-face, but the performance is consistent throughout the year.\u201d\n\nBeyond awards, the event reinforced a maturing global model defined by accountability, trust, and integration. As hybrid work becomes permanent, companies are prioritising performance and reliability over proximity, and Sri Lanka\u2019s technical depth and communication maturity have positioned it as a strategic hub for international organisations.\n\nScale Up 2026 was not simply an anniversary celebration. It marked a shift from proving the distributed model to scaling it, with deeper AI capability, stronger finance integration, and a unified Group structure designed for the next decade of global growth."
